      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISS SUPERNOVA (2) returns after a 21-week break. Opened last prep with a second to Agatha over 1100m at the Kensington circuit. Has trialled twice recently and looks set for a positive opening to the prep. OAKFIELD VIRGINIA (3) had her first run in 14 months over this trip at Scone recently and caught the eye in the run home, getting up for second. Has talent and that last hit-out will do her the world of good. TESTAMAPATIENCE (6) raced midfield and was fair through the line on debut over 1100m at Rosehill last time out. Should do a little better over the extra 100m. The Waterhouse/Bott-trained SINGLE LADIES (5) resumes and sees a dry track for the first time. Can improve on what we saw last prep. Early favourite is Frankel filly RISHAKA (4) on debut for Waller with McDonald to ride. Had a quiet trial recently but there will obviously be a buzz around this runner.",
